    <string name="section_about">About Black Glass</string>
    <string name="about_note">A minimal offline launcher: no internet permission, no ads, no tracking. Everything stays on this phone.</string>
    <string name="search_names_note">Your own names for apps: long-press an app in the search results.</string>
    <string name="battery_profiles_note">Background restriction (“Restricted” in battery settings) is set per app for the whole phone — Android does not let launchers change it per profile. Open an app’s battery settings from its menu: long press in search → App info.</string>
    <string name="grid_hint">Apps on the home screen: long-press an icon and drag it to any place — top, centre, a corner. If another app is there, they swap. Each profile has its own layout.</string>
    <string name="sms_help_title">How to turn on SMS search</string>
    <string name="sms_help_new">Android 15 and newer (and some Android 13–14 phones), when Black Glass is not installed from Play: Android blocks SMS access until you allow it. 1) Try to turn on “SMS” above once. 2) Open the Black Glass app info (button below). 3) Tap ⋮ in the top right → “Allow restricted settings” and confirm with your PIN or fingerprint. 4) Come back and turn on “SMS” again.</string>
    <string name="sms_help_old">Android 14 and older: just turn on “SMS” above and allow access when asked.</string>
